message: "If you use this software, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Resonate AI Mesh: a deterministic, replayable research instrument for multi-agent decisions under the Pordenone kernel"
type: software
authors:
  - name: Vers3Dynamics
repository-code: "https://github.com/topherchris420/resonate-ai-mesh"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-03"
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - deterministic replay
  - bounded judgment
  - human oversight
  - reproducible experiments
abstract: >-
  Research software in which simulated agents propose actions and a
  deterministic kernel decides: validation first, optional bounded judgment,
  versioned policy, then a single authorized mutation path. Every run is a
  hash-chained event log that can be verified independently, replayed
  without network access, explained decision by decision, and branched into
  counterfactuals. Experiments use paired repetitions, pre-registered
  predictions, interval estimates, and effect sizes; claims are checked
  against recorded evidence. All human-state data is simulated. The software
  does not control physical systems.
